{"type":"message","id":"9d4a958b","parentId":"6d71ff7e","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:47:07.056Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Error 1101 is a Cloudflare Workers error - it means the Worker script has crashed or hit a resource limit. This is a server-side issue, not a client-side issue. Let me try GET /health or GET /status to see if the server is still running.\n\nActually, the GET endpoints work fine but POST doesn't. This could be a server-side issue with the POST handler. Let me try GET /send or some other endpoint.\n\nWait, maybe the endpoint is different? Let me check if there's a different POST endpoint or if there's something I'm missing. Maybe the send endpoint is /message or /post?\n\nLet me also try to see if there are any other endpoints.\n\nActually, error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker exceeded resource limits\". This is a server-side issue - the Worker script is crashing when trying to handle POST requests. This is not something I can fix on the client side.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-b1ea088f-830b-4d82-85e5-0aa1de345792","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/health\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-c0f14446-dd75-4494-ab52-6cf283747870","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/status\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":274,"output":297,"cacheRead":19616,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20187,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778986017187,"responseId":"chatcmpl-7abefb2c-6ff7-46aa-956d-e1e85e0167b7"}}
